[1746057600,-24.46],[1748736000,-23.89],[1751328000,-16.23],[1754006400,-4.74],[1756684800,-10.31],[1759276800,-4.8],[1761955200,-2.46],[1764547200,1.74],[1767225600,5.23],[1769904000,6.15],[1772323200,-5.37],[1775001600,-14.38],[1777593600,5.65],[1780272000,3.24]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What does the Foreign Tourist Arrivals data represent?","answer":"Foreign Tourist Arrivals (FTA) data quantifies the number of visitors from other countries during a specific period who enter India for a variety of purposes, such as leisure, business, or education, excluding those who come for employment.^This metric is crucial for understanding India’s tourism industry's reach and impact. FTAs are often counted on the basis of border entry data and provide a clear picture of the international popularity and attractiveness of a destination."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Foreign Tourist Arrivals data?","answer":"Foreign Tourist Arrivals are a key economic indicator for the tourism sector, directly impacting revenues from tourism and related services.^High FTA numbers reflect global interest in a country's culture, history, and natural beauty, promoting cultural exchange and international understanding.^FTA data indicates emerging trends in global tourism, such as shifts in traveller preferences or the rising popularity of certain destinations.^Fluctuations in FTA can reflect the effectiveness of tourism policies, marketing campaigns, and global perceptions of a country.^A thriving tourism sector indicated by high FTAs can be a significant source of employment, both directly in tourism and indirectly in associated sectors.^Foreign Tourist Arrivals can have a broad socio-economic impact, including on local businesses, heritage site maintenance, and regional development.^Governments use Foreign Tourist Arrivals data for tourism policy making, infrastructure development, and promotional activities."},{"question":"How to interpret the Foreign Tourist Arrivals data?","answer":"A consistent increase in FTAs is usually a sign of a healthy and growing tourism sector, while a decline might indicate underlying issues or global trends affecting travel.^High FTA numbers might necessitate improvements in infrastructure and services to accommodate growing tourist numbers, impacting urban planning and development."}],"related":[{"slug":"baltic-dry-index","title":"Baltic Dry Index"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"external-commercial-borrowings-ecbs","title":"External Commercial Borrowings (ECBs)"},{"slug":"foreign-exchange-reserves","title":"Foreign Exchange Reserves"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-direct-investment-fdi","title":"Gross Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)"},{"slug":"gross-foreign-portfolio-investment-fpi","title":"Gross Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI)"},{"slug":"import-cover-months","title":"Import Cover (Months)"},{"slug":"international-air-passenger-traffic","title":"Air Passenger Traffic - International"},{"slug":"non-oil-exports","title":"Non-Oil Exports"},{"slug":"port-cargo-traffic","title":"Port Cargo Traffic"},{"slug":"services-trade-net-inflows","title":"Services Trade- Net Inflows"}],"title":"Foreign Tourist Arrivals","description":"India's foreign tourist arrivals stand at 3.24% for Jun 2026. Tourist arrivals feed directly into services exports and the net services surplus.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's foreign tourist arrivals stand at 3.24% for Jun 2026. Tourist arrivals feed directly into services exports and the net services surplus."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-06-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-19T15:06:08+00:00"}